Path 1: Google Sheet (Static Storage)
The sheet acts as the primary database. If the webhook is blocked or rate-limited, the sheet retains the data.

Open Google Drive. Create a new, blank Google Sheet. Name it whatever you want (e.g., Logs).

Look at the browser URL. It will look like this:
https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1aBcDeFgHiJkLmNoPqRsTuVwXyZ1234567890/edit

Extract the string between /d/ and /edit. In the example above, the ID is 1aBcDeFgHiJkLmNoPqRsTuVwXyZ1234567890.

Open your Code.gs in Google Apps Script. Find this line:
var sheetId = "YOUR_GOOGLE_SHEET_ID_HERE";

Replace the placeholder with your ID:
var sheetId = "1aBcDeFgHiJkLmNoPqRsTuVwXyZ1234567890";

Path 2: Discord Webhook (Real-Time Push)
The webhook pushes the captured data directly to your phone or desktop in real-time.

Open Discord. Create a private server (or use an existing one you control).

Go to Server Settings -> Integrations -> Webhooks.

Click New Webhook. Select the channel you want the data to drop into.

Click Copy Webhook URL. It will look like:
https://discord.com/api/webhooks/123456789012345678/AbCdEfGhIjKlMnOpQrStUvWxYz

Open your Code.gs. Find this line:
var webhookUrl = "YOUR_DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL_HERE";

Replace the placeholder with your URL:
var webhookUrl = "https://discord.com/api/webhooks/123456789012345678/AbCdEfGhIjKlMnOpQrStUvWxYz";

Execution and Scope Authorization
Once both strings are replaced in Code.gs, save the file (Ctrl + S).

The critical step:
You must trigger the authorization flow before the script will work.

In the Apps Script editor, look at the top toolbar. Select processForm from the dropdown menu next to the "Debug" (bug icon) button.

Click Run.

Google will prompt: "Authorization required. This project requires your permission to access data."

Click Review Permissions, choose your account, click Advanced, and click Go to [Project Name] (unsafe).

Google will ask for permission to:

See, edit, create, and delete all your Google Sheets spreadsheets (for the Sheet ID).

Connect to an external service (for the Discord webhook).

Click Allow.

The connections are now live. When the Index.html form is submitted via the deployed Web App, data flows to both points simultaneously.

